+/*
+ * SAGIT (Xiaomi Mi 6, MSM8998) Adreno 540 CP bring-up -- stage 3.
+ *
+ * Stages 1 and 2 proved that this kernel can talk to the secure monitor and
+ * that the monitor accepts the a540 zap image (PAS init_image / mem_setup /
+ * auth_and_reset all returned 0), after which RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL reads
+ * 0x1 and the GPU is out of secure mode.  This stage is the first one that
+ * asks the command processor to do something:
+ *
+ *   power the GPU block far enough to touch it (idempotent; the probe may
+ *   already have done it), copy a530_pfp.fw / a530_pm4.fw into the reserved
+ *   low region, point CP_PFP_INSTR_BASE / CP_PM4_INSTR_BASE at them, set up
+ *   a 4 KiB ring and a 4 KiB indirect buffer, un-halt the ME, submit the
+ *   8-dword CP_ME_INIT packet, then submit one CP_MEM_WRITE through the IB
+ *   and poll for the 32-bit word it writes.  The word is read back through
+ *   the kernel's own mapping: if it holds "CPOK" the CP fetched its
+ *   microcode, parsed the ring, fetched the IB and executed a packet.
+ *
+ * Off unless sweetcp=1.  Non-fatal: every failure is one line and the boot
+ * continues.
+ *
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * What is proven and where it was read
+ *
+ * The CP register map is the A5xx one.  Byte offset = dword offset << 2
+ * (kgsl: adreno.c:2358 `base + (offsetwords << 2)`; the mainline XML and
+ * generated a5xx.xml.h are dword offsets too):
+ *
+ *   CP_RB_BASE            0x800    a5xx_reg.h:60 / a5xx.xml.h:915
+ *   CP_RB_BASE_HI         0x801
+ *   CP_RB_CNTL            0x802
+ *   CP_RB_RPTR            0x806    (RB_RPTR_ADDR is 0x804/0x805, unused here)
+ *   CP_RB_WPTR            0x807
+ *   CP_ROQ_THRESHOLDS_1   0x81f
+ *   CP_ROQ_THRESHOLDS_2   0x820
+ *   CP_MEQ_THRESHOLDS     0x825
+ *   CP_MERCIU_SIZE        0x826
+ *   CP_ME_CNTL            0x832    kgsl name; mainline calls it
+ *                                  CP_PFP_ME_CNTL (a5xx.xml.h:983).  Bit 0 is
+ *                                  ME_HALT: "clear ME_HALT to start the micro
+ *                                  engine" (adreno_a5xx.c:2493).
+ *   CP_PFP_INSTR_BASE_LO  0x835 / _HI 0x836
+ *   CP_PM4_INSTR_BASE_LO  0x838 / _HI 0x839
+ *   CP_ADDR_MODE_CNTL     0x860    (1 = 64-bit GPU addresses)
+ *   CP_ME_STAT_DATA       0xb14
+ *   CP_WFI_PEND_CTR       0xb15
+ *   CP_INTERRUPT_STATUS   0xb18
+ *   CP_HW_FAULT           0xb1a
+ *   CP_AHB_FAULT          0xb1b
+ *   CP_PROTECT_STATUS     0xb1c
+ *   CP_IB1_BASE           0xb1f / _HI 0xb20 / CP_IB1_BUFSZ 0xb21
+ *   RBBM_STATUS           0x4f5    (bit 6 CP_BUSY, bit 30 GPU busy CP)
+ *   RBBM_AHB_ERROR_STATUS 0x4f4
+ *   RBBM_AHB_CNTL0        0x093 / RBBM_AHB_CNTL1 0x094
+ *
+ * The init sequence is the vendor's, not a guess.  kgsl a5xx_rb_start()
+ * (adreno_a5xx.c:2464-2520) does, in this order: CP_RB_CNTL, CP_RB_BASE,
+ * a5xx_microcode_load(), CP_ME_CNTL = 0, then a5xx_send_me_init() which
+ * puts a CP_ME_INIT type-7 packet (8 dwords) in the ring and spins for up
+ * to 2000 ms.  a5xx_hw_init() before it programs the queue thresholds:
+ * for A540/A512 (adreno_a5xx.c:1963-1970) CP_MEQ_THRESHOLDS = 0x40,
+ * CP_MERCIU_SIZE = 0x400, CP_ROQ_THRESHOLDS_2 = 0x80000060,
+ * CP_ROQ_THRESHOLDS_1 = 0x40201B16, and sets CP_ADDR_MODE_CNTL = 1
+ * (mainline a5xx_hw_init(), a5xx_gpu.c:917).
+ *
+ * a5xx_microcode_load() (adreno_a5xx.c:2233-2300) is only four register
+ * writes: CP_PM4_INSTR_BASE_LO/HI and CP_PFP_INSTR_BASE_LO/HI, pointing at
+ * the microcode buffers.  There is NO scratch-register upload on A5xx:
+ * CP_ME_NRT_ADDR (0x80d) / CP_ME_NRT_DATA (0x810) exist in the mainline
+ * register map but this kernel's a5xx_reg.h does not even declare them and
+ * kgsl never writes them for a5xx -- that is the A3xx/A4xx "ME RAM" load
+ * path.  The microcode "version" word (fw->data[4]) is likewise only
+ * reported to userspace/snapshots; it is not written to any register.
+ *
+ * The CP_ME_INIT payload is the vendor's _set_ordinals() result for a540v2
+ * (adreno_a5xx.c:2310-2390, _me_init_ucode_workarounds() 0x00000000 for
+ * patchid != 0; the DT's qcom,chipid 0x05040001 has patchid 1).  Mainline
+ * a5xx_me_init() writes the identical eight dwords for a540.
+ *
+ * The ring header is the type-7 packet header from adreno_pm4types.h:
+ * (7 << 28) | count | odd-parity(count) << 15 | (opcode & 0x7f) << 16 |
+ * odd-parity(opcode) << 23 -- NOT the "opcode << 8" shape one might expect
+ * from older Adreno generations.  CP_ME_INIT is opcode 0x48
+ * (adreno_pm4types.h:40), CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER_PFE 0x3f, CP_MEM_WRITE 0x3d.
+ *
+ * The firmware header is decoded by mi6/sagit/tools/mkcpfw.py and repeated
+ * in bsd/dev/sweet_cp_image.c; kgsl drops the file's first dword and copies
+ * the rest, so the image the CP sees starts with the version word.
+ *
+ * What is inferred, not proven
+ *
+ *  - 64-bit microcode instructions at image dword 2 (8-byte aligned after
+ *    the 2-dword version/table-offset header).  The arithmetic fits
+ *    perfectly (code = table_offset - 2 dwords, table = 128 dwords) and the
+ *    instruction-looking dwords have an 8-byte period, but no disassembler
+ *    was run on a530_pfp.fw.
+ *  - A 4 KiB ring is legal: CP_RB_CNTL.BUFSZ is log2(ring bytes / 8), which
+ *    mainline and kgsl agree on (mainline uses 32 KiB -> 12; kgsl's
+ *    A5XX_CP_RB_CNTL_DEFAULT is the same field from KGSL_RB_DWORDS).  The
+ *    hardware's minimum size is not documented in either tree.
+ *  - The GPU is not in a translating SMMU context.  See the SMMU section in
+ *    mi6/docs/4k/cp-ringbuffer.md: this stage programs no SMMU, so the CP
+ *    must be seeing physical addresses.  sCR0 reads 0x00200626 on the
+ *    phone, i.e. SMMUEN=1, and no S2CR/CBAR has been programmed by this
+ *    kernel; if the TZ did not leave the GPU's stream IDs bypassed the
+ *    first fetch (the microcode at CP_PFP_INSTR_BASE) will fault.  The log
+ *    is built to say which of those happened.
+ *
+ * Boot args (default off; a plain boot is unchanged):
+ *   sweetcp=1            run this stage
+ *   sweetcpdelay=<s>     seconds to wait first, 1..180, default 40.  It
+ *                        must run after the zap (default 20 s) in the same
+ *                        boot: without the zap the GPU is still secure and
+ *                        the CP cannot fetch non-secure microcode.
+ *
+ * Report, log lines and failure signatures: mi6/docs/4k/cp-ringbuffer.md.
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ */
+
